  "rationale": "A2.4D requires the full chain standard form → vertex form → attributes. Fidelity V2 therefore makes every family begin with standard form, requires the complete vertex form, and then grades attributes such as vertex, axis, extrema, opening, or range. Completing-square evidence is collected repeatedly, including cases with |a|>1 and a genuine factoring error repair.",
  "documents": [
    {
