          "solutionReview": {
            "headline": "A half-integer vertex makes the arithmetic harder without changing the completing-square procedure.",
            "reasoning": [
              "After factoring 4, the inside x-coefficient is {{innerB}}.",
              "Half of that coefficient is {{negH}}, so the square-add value is {{squareAdd}}.",
              "The completed form is $4(x-({{h}}))^2+({{k}})$."
            ],
            "answerSummary": "Vertex $({{h}},{{k}})$ with axis $x={{h}}$."
          },
          "attemptFeedback": [
            "Factor the 4 before halving the inside x-coefficient."
